%N A401368 Number of ways to write 2n as p + q with p a twin prime and q a cousin prime.
%C A401368 Here a twin prime is a prime p with p-2 or p+2 prime (A001097), and a cousin prime is a prime q with q-4 or q+4 prime (A023200, A046132).
%C A401368 Conjecture: a(n) > 0 for all n > 2, i.e., every even number greater than 4 is the sum of a twin prime and a cousin prime. Verified for 2n <= 3.4*10^10.
%e A401368 a(15) = 5: 30 = 7 + 23 = 11 + 19 = 13 + 17 = 17 + 13 = 19 + 11.
%o A401368 (PARI) tw(p)=isprime(p)&&(isprime(p+2)||(p>2&&isprime(p-2)))
%o A401368 co(p)=isprime(p)&&(isprime(p+4)||(p>4&&isprime(p-4)))
%o A401368 a(n)=sum(p=2, 2*n-2, tw(p)&&co(2*n-p))
%o A401368 (Python)
%o A401368 from sympy import isprime
%o A401368 def co(p): return isprime(p) and (isprime(p+4) or (p > 4 and isprime(p-4)))
%o A401368 def tw(p): return isprime(p) and (isprime(p+2) or (p > 2 and isprime(p-2)))
%o A401368 def a(n): return sum(1 for p in range(2, 2*n-1) if tw(p) and co(2*n-p))
%Y A401368 Cf. A001097, A023200, A046132, A002375, A007534.
%K A401368 nonn,new
%O A401368 1,5
